  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EABRN 2024-2026</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The East Asian Biosphere Reserve Network (EABRN) is a regional network supporting UNESCO&apos;s MAB Programme and was initially established with three priority themes for cooperation: eco-tourism, conservation policy, and trans- boundary cooperation. EABRN was officially launched in 1995 by China, the Democratic People&apos;s Republic of Korea (DPRK), Japan, Mongolia and the Republic of Korea (ROK), who were joined by the Russian Federation in 1998 and Kazakhstan in 2011. The overall goal/objective of the project is sustain a strong and active network of well-managed BRs across the seven EABRN member countries, actively engaging in bilateral and multilateral exchanges on management, research and local development and defining the sub-regional implementation of the new Hangzhou Action Plan (2026-2035).</narrative>
  </description>
